      "id": "l1",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "How a bond works",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "How a bond works"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/1-jak-dziala-obligacja.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "When you buy a bond, **you lend money** to the issuer. In return you get:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                "**Interest (coupon)** – regularly",
                "**The amount back** – on the maturity date"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Before maturity the bond's price changes: when **rates rise**, old bond prices **fall**, and when rates fall – they rise."
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "Hold to maturity and the issuer doesn't go bankrupt? You get **the full amount**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
